<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mahisagar district</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mahisagar district is a district of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, created in 2013 from parts of the Panchmahal and Kheda districts, with its headquarters at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lunavada">Lunavada</a>. It is named after the Mahi river, which flows through it. Its territory includes the former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a> of Lunavada, Sant and Balasinor.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mahisagar-district.jpg" alt="Mahisagar district" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tejash.my26 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Restored_Hindu_Shrine_at_Kaleshwari,_Gujarat,_India.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
